  "all_findings": [
    {
      "id": "F-G-DISPATCH",
      "severity": "severe",
      "title": "Catalog techniques garch / gjr_garch / egarch did not auto-inject `vol` based on technique_id; egarch UI invocations silently produced vanilla GARCH math",
      "details": "Phase 1 exploration found that resources/catalog/techniques_catalog.json defines 3 separate techniques (garch, gjr_garch, egarch) but none expose `vol` as a user-visible param. The wrapper's run() function read ctx.get_param('vol', 'GARCH') and defaulted to plain GARCH when `vol` was absent. Sweep 0 verified pre-fix: technique_id='egarch' with catalog-default params {p:1, q:1, dist:'t'} produced model='GARCH' (not 'EGARCH') with o=0 and AIC=2723.80 \u2014 identical to vanilla GARCH math, NOT EGARCH. Same cell post-fix produces model='EGARCH' with o=1 and AIC=2723.19. GJR-GARCH was less affected because the catalog passes o=1 explicitly so the math (asymmetry-leverage term) was correct via arch_model's o param even with vol defaulting; but the displayed model_label was 'GARCH' not 'GJR-GARCH', a labeling inconsistency. Fix applied inline in this session: 5 LOC at top of engine/techniques/garch_model.py:run() that resolves technique_id \u2192 variant default for `vol` BEFORE the user-param read, so explicit user `vol` still wins. Within CAL-R6 (\u226450 LOC \u22642 files inline).",
      "fix_status": "fixed_inline",
      "fix_location": "engine/techniques/garch_model.py lines 92-105 (_TID_VOL_MAP injection)"
    }
  ]
